Here is the root cause:
The dualpi2_change() function's while loop for enforcing limit/memlimit unconditionally dequeued from the root qdisc (C-queue) without checking if the C-queue was empty or if the L-queue contained packets. When packets were only in the L-queue, it called qdisc_dequeue_internal(sch, true) which returned NULL because the root qdisc was empty, leading to a NULL skb dereference. Additionally, the return value was not checked, so the subsequent operations on skb caused a crash. The fix properly drains both queues and checks return values.

